    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n102303" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τᾰνηλεγής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
		perh. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bringing long woe</i>,
			epith. of death, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μοῖρα τανηλεγέος θανάτοιο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					2.100
				</span></i>
			, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δύο κῆρε τ. θ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				8.70
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κὴρ . . τ. θ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				11.171
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Tyrt.
				12.35
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τανηλεγέως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Supp.Epigr.</u>
					1.450
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Phrygia</span>). (Apparently a compd. of
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλγος </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλέγω</span>) 
				like
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυσηλεγής</span>
			.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
